A watch is set through a thread capability without the right to control the thread,
so whoever may only name a thread decides who hears its faults.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call set the watch of a thread its caller could not control

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -734,7 +734,7 @@ static int dispatch(struct thread *t, uint32_t op, uint32_t slot, uint32_t *arg)
         err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_process(t, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         break;
     case CAP_THREAD:
-        err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_thread(t, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
+        err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) || op == OP_THREAD_WATCH ? op_thread(t, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         break;
     case CAP_NOTIFICATION:
         err = op_notification(t, &cap, op, arg);
